{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>I feared</b> — ד׳ (four) times. And the rest: 'I passed over the disgrace that I feared.' 'And that which I feared has come upon me' (Job 3:25). יגרתי — 'all my sorrows I knew' — that You would not acquit me. יגדתי — because of the anger and the wrath. And I prayed that You pass over my disgrace, lest the nations say etc. 'And that which I feared has come upon me' — meaning: to me alone, for even though You heard my prayer on behalf of Israel, You did not acquit me, and You decreed that I die in the wilderness and not enter the Land."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:09:18.837052691Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}